{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1463938-evolved-psiads","id":1463938,"title":"Evolved psiads.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-14T20:14:32-07:00","id":1463938,"title":"Evolved psiads.","content":"Let's assume that a doyen for some reason created a prometheus chamber to just generally enhance the psionic capability of humanity, a psiad based chamber, applying the same boost psions got. Or, it you want, it was a crazy alien gadget, or maybe even the bad cheese someone ate last night.<br /> <br /> But ultimately, what would &quot;evolved&quot; psiads look like? how would they differ from psions, if both were in the same setting?<br /> <br /> My first thought is that they still don't get the easy ways to combine powers psions get, so that even if they can access higher tiers of power than &quot;natural&quot; psiads, they still run into issues compared to a group of psions working together. Another possibility might be higher limit in terms of dot cap for various psionic modes.<br /> <br /> What dost thou think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T20:21:40-07:00","id":1463940,"title":"","content":"I think the most likely answer you\u2019re going to get is that they\u2019ll look like psions with whatever limitation individual readers don\u2019t like removed. (Or looking at it another way, they\u2019ll look just like psiads but remove any limitations individuals don\u2019t like.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T03:58:38-07:00","id":1464353,"title":"","content":"Well, I suppose that the advanced psions would be created by enhanced and uncapped Prometheus Chambers. so, I'd say it'd be something greater than current psiads, greater than the psions, and equal/lesser to the Doyen. <br /> <br /> The example Doyens do not have 7 in every mode. What's strange, since the doyen did make the chambers that got the proxies 7 psi and 7 in all their preferred modes - all at once. Either the doyen got much better in psionic and genetic theory after they botched their ascensions (and could make a chamber that made 7s in all modes in all aptitudes), or (less boringly), there is a hard limit on how many 7s you can get. From that, I can say the advanced psiads shouldn't be able to reach 7 in every conceivable mode due to whatever chamber and genetic advancements. <br /> <br /> Psiads would have the support bonuses that psions have, from the chambers, and would be able to do enhance themselves with different aptitudes. (By the way, I assume that the doyen are able to do the same.) They also would be able to do many combination effects from these aptitudes, for extra flexibility (such as the biokinesys/vitakinesys combo for permanent changes).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T05:11:33-07:00","id":1464357,"title":"","content":"If it was I who would describe the next step of psiad evolution, I would allow Psiads to reach Psi 7 and 5 dots in every mode.<br /> <br /> Than, you have Favored Aptitude and Strong Mode that allow you to reach 6 dot in a single mode.<br /> <br /> I would make new Psionic Edges, one that allow you to increase by 1 dot all the modes of their favorite aptitude (what would allow you to reach 7 in a mode with Strong Mode), one that align the amount of psi points the psiad get with what psions get, and 1 that allow the psiad to empower each other like psions do (considering the psiad as a Psion of the same aptitude as their Favorite Aptitude)<br /> <br /> That set of small steps would put a psiad in the same level as a Doyen (7 in one aptitude and 5 in all the others)<br /> <br /> Edit: I would not change the XP cost of psiads. Psion are genetically enchanted to become masters in their aptitude, what is not the case for psiads.<br /> <br /> Additionally, I would make all children of psions be automatically psiads capable of reaching psi 7, but the slow evolution would point them to enter the chamber to empower themselves (make it easier to evolve), as no one really knows how far they can go without a chamber.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 10-18-2021, 08:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T11:12:28-07:00","id":1464394,"title":"","content":"This has always been something of a curiosity for me, specifically why it doesn't exist already (in certain circles). A skilled biokinetic Psiad who has (maybe with some vitakinesis?) who has examined a Psion) should? be able to make many of the improvements on themselves without the limitations (and they can experiment temporarily until they get it right).<br /> <br /> Slightly more difficult, but still possible a skilled biokinetic Psion who has examined a Psiad, should be able to find a way to reconnect the natural pathways etc. again they can experiment temporarily before making the changes permanent.<br /> <br /> I know it is hinted at in the books that the biokinetics are working toward this...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","name":"econclark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T11:44:30-07:00","id":1464396,"title":"","content":"Psi is not exactly covered by BK, it is in VK (in the case of increasing personal Psi value), and you need 5 dots in Augends to increase it partially and temporarily. What is beyond all but a Psi 6 Psiad with strong mode (Augendis), a absolutely precise situation very hard to get with a very limited number of Psiads.<br /> <br /> Maybe QK could help there using Fundamental, but QK was out of Psiad reach until 2104, and there are not that many Psiads around the world.<br /> <br /> A second point is, until the Psions show up, the understanding of Psi and how it is different from Quantum was limited to very few people (some Terats and high Escalon \u00c6on). Most Psiads would see themselves as Novas/Aberrants and would hide their powers in the risk of persecution and death, and even those that know they are not Aberrants, would still be afraid if being seen as one. Practicing powers is the only way to Psiads evolve, and hiding it is not the easiest way to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T13:56:54-07:00","id":1464416,"title":"","content":"Psi may not be precisely covered, but the changes made by the prometheous chambers are...I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","name":"econclark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T14:10:36-07:00","id":1464417,"title":"","content":"The boundary between BK and VK are thin and diffused, so it\u2019s hard to say no, but in the mode descriptions the only way to increase Psi is using VK.<br /> <br /> I would say BK (if used in another character) would change the biological/DNA factor of the character, but the Chamber has a noetic template changing component that BK can\u2019t change, while VK can (to certain degree), and can do all the required changes by the,selves (if powerful enough).<br /> <br /> But there are 3 different conditions here, we have Latents, Psions and Psiads, transforming a Latent into a Psion is not just a matter of only biology, so BK would not be capable anyway, maybe a strong latent could be changed in a way that they can evolve into a psiad by themselves later (big question mark there), and maybe it\u2019s possible to break the limits of a psion using BK (another big question mark there).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T14:58:12-07:00","id":1464421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>econclark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1463938-evolved-psiads?p=1464394#post1464394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This has always been something of a curiosity for me, specifically why it doesn't exist already (in certain circles). A skilled biokinetic Psiad who has (maybe with some vitakinesis?) who has examined a Psion) should? be able to make many of the improvements on themselves without the limitations (and they can experiment temporarily until they get it right).<br /> <br /> Slightly more difficult, but still possible a skilled biokinetic Psion who has examined a Psiad, should be able to find a way to reconnect the natural pathways etc. again they can experiment temporarily before making the changes permanent.</div> </div> </div> </div>One difficulty is that Psiads don't really get the high level powers that'd allow for permanent changes until they reach Psi 5 or 6, and I doubt many Psiads have hit those milestones.<br /> <br /> It takes Iatrosis 5 (requiring Psi 6 and an Edge) to make permanent adjustments to someone's underlying noetic template, and even then you cannot grant or remove psionic power; although combining efforts with a Biokinetic may help in that regard.<br /> <br /> Another would be that Psiads are trying to hide, so generally avoid Psions; they certainly wouldn't want to draw attention by performing a deep genetic scan of a Psion. A successful scan would potentially reveal what Nippon's researchers already know, that Psions contain alien DNA. Would a Psiad looking for a power boost be willing to incorporate alien DNA of unknown origin into themself, especially when commercially available bioapps (also containing alien DNA) can already boost their powers in a variety of ways?<br /> <br /> There is also the possibility that a Psiad trying to incorporate Psion genetics into themself could either cripple some Aptitudes while boosting another or inadvertently gain the telepathic backdoor put in place by the Doyen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T15:10:03-07:00","id":1464422,"title":"","content":"If a Psiad is passing off rather than just plain hiding...they would have plenty of opportunity to scan their fellows...in which case they may be like...huh maybe that is what gives them that boost let me try...works? maybe if yes make the changes permanent as most/all are DNA based I think. They may also be able to find and break the mental/genetic/psionic barrier put in place by the Doyen on the Psions...Vitakinetics would also be very helpful here...<br /> <br /> Also, could a skilled Vitakinetic take a Psion that has been through the Prometheous chamber and turn them back to a neutral (like they could with a amphibious human?) I don't see why not, but it seems bad to say yes.<br /> <br /> It is true I don't think they could turn latents into psiads,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","name":"econclark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T15:24:43-07:00","id":1464423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>econclark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1463938-evolved-psiads?p=1464422#post1464422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, could a skilled Vitakinetic take a Psion that has been through the Prometheous chamber and turn them back to a neutral (like they could with a amphibious human?) I don't see why not, but it seems bad to say yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Adjust Template power specifically doesn't let you do that. Page 262:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">In addition, this power cannot be used to create </span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">or remove psionic latency or powers, affect Corruption, </span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">or change whether someone is an Aberrant or a Talent.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>At best I'd turn the attempt into an opposed roll, with successes counting as a Complication to buy off before the target can freely use their powers.<br /> <br /> If the target truly <i>wanted</i> to be rid of their powers, I'd let it work, but follow the rules for using the power to perform a sex change:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The patient must voluntarily consent to </span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">changes, otherwise they revert to their previous state. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The patient can rescind his consent for up to a month </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">after the changes have been made.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","user":"Shepherdboi","date":". 10-18-2021, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T07:40:16-08:00","id":1474977,"title":"","content":"The first issue I see in this scenario, is that aside from the Doyen, in-universe, there are very few people who could envision this, let alone achieve it, and the Doyens have a marked interest in making sure it never ever happens, and have consistently hobbled the scientific and psi development of other alien races to an even greater degree than they've done to humans.<br /> <br /> So you'd need access to high-level noetic science that was never influenced by the Doyen (like the one that possessed poor Sara Kaur precisely to make sure humans never uncovered something that might make them too powerful). The ideal moment to escape Doyen sabotage to achieve this is paradoxically before the Aeon era, since Doyen oversight might have been lesser, but the scientific knowledge to do it would have been unavailable and would have to be achieved from the ground up, which would take a *long* time (or that knowledge could be discreetly stolen from other advanced psi aliens with a clairvoyance/teleportation/telepathy combo).<br /> <br /> If your goal is a super-psiad, I don't think by the RAW any power achievable by an &quot;unevolved&quot; psiad could conceivably &quot;pop the locks&quot;, because unlike psions, psiads don't actually have any locks, they're just limited by their own unrefined potential. So the issue is how to &quot;evolve&quot; a psiad, which is markedly different from unlocking something that's already there. It would require superscience and given that it took supergenius Sara Kaur almost 2 centuries to just unlock QK, I don't know what it would take to effectively compress millenias of human evolution, but it should be beyond the current scope of humanity. Maybe a super-intelligent nova could figure it out, but why would they bother trying to ?<br /> <br /> If your goal is a super-psion, assuming regular psions know to and manage to escape Doyen surveillance somehow, I expect that it's a matter of regrowing what psionic pathways the Doyen amputated with their regular prometheus chambers. So I would say, you'd need psion scientists working in concert figuring it out. At least one (but most likely several) geneticist and noeticist with clairsentience on steroids using Omniscience to observe alien and human DNA strands and figure out the subquantum interactions between psi and human biology necessary to boost human psi without limiting its versatility. And then getting around whatever genetic boobytraps the Doyen likely arranged to keep humans from doing just that. <br /> <br /> Once he figures out what to do, he either needs a telepath to convey to a proxy-like VK the super-sophisticated alterations that should be made to a psion's template to implement the &quot;jailbreak codes&quot; to his full abilities, or more likely he needs brilliant EK and VK engineers to help him build a bioware &quot;jailbreaking&quot; chamber.<br /> <br /> And since that guy (or those guys) is not a Doyen relying on millenias of knowledge of supernoetics, even with Intelligence 6 or 7 it might take him a while to achieve limited results (a psion with 2 main aptitudes (3 if you count QK) and auxiliary modes up to 3 or 4). Anything beyond that would for me be grossly excessive, because psi transcendance should still be out of reach for humanity. I don't think we currently know with any accuracy where the limit stands between &quot;the Doyen didn't want humanity too powerful&quot; and &quot;there's a limit to how much we can overclock these primitive lifeforms even if we graft on them some of our DNA&quot;.<br /> <br /> As always, YMMV<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26426-trianoma4evah","name":"Trianoma4Evah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T10:37:21-08:00","id":1474990,"title":"","content":"In my head cannon, Bhurano didn\u2019t unlock QK purposefully, she was experimenting with some psi hardtech that used QK Fundamentals mode (it\u2019s not impossible to create other Aptitudes supertech, just hard), and it creates a new wave of waking powers, but now in the form of Psiads and latents, instead of Novas as Mal did. When she did it, the QK gene was unlocked too, and she probably got the most powerful blast, allowing her to unlock it faster and maybe giving her +1Psi.<br /> <br /> In my head cannon too, she was not Psi 6 until that moment, and she was probably the most powerful Psiad around in the time, so most Psiads were Psi 3-4 in Nova era, what puts them in the same level as Talents.<br /> <br /> Back to QK, I would say Doyen while incapable of developing QK themselves, developed QK supertech, powerful enough to create the bounce around earth, that Mal would destroy in N-Day, also, killing a doyen is almost impossible without QK, so they probably had some kind of QK supertech to kill their offspring and the other doyens that went crazy.<br /> <br /> All that to say, while the Doyen did restrain human psi development, they restrain a few steps ahead of what would be the limits before. Without the doyen there would be a few hundred Psiads instead of many thousand Psions, the power level would be around psi 3-4 with a few caping to 5 and maybe Bhurano as the unique psi 6 Psiads, while doyens allowed thousands of psi 4-5 and hundreds of psi 6.<br /> <br /> in other words, are Doyen good? NO, absolutely not\u2026 did they help? Yes, a lot!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T13:15:28-08:00","id":1475004,"title":"","content":"I don't think Doyen would even be capable of creating an evolved Psiad, even if they wanted to. And I don't think they'd want to. Aren't Psion's basically just applying a Doyen template on humans? A Doyen template that was purposefully weakened, as well. But even if the Doyen made a Prometheus Chamber that didn't purposefully give out flawed templates the Doyen seem much more focused in their psionic abilities then Humans can potentially become.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T15:23:36-08:00","id":1475007,"title":"","content":"No.<br /> <br /> Doyens can go 7 dots in one Aptitude and 5 dots in all others Aptitudes (except QK, that they can\u2019t learn), while going up to Psi 7. It\u2019s on Aeon, page 360.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T18:36:06-08:00","id":1475011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Planguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1463938-evolved-psiads?p=1475004#post1475004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren't Psion's basically just applying a Doyen template on humans?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. The fact that non-Quantakinetic psions have the potential to develop Quantakinetic auxiliary modes is proof the Doyen didn't just use a genetic cut and paste.<br /> <br /> Going back to the thread's original post, what an evolved psiad looks like depends on the specific point in their evolution. They'd presumably (over generations or via genetic manipulation) gain some combination of cheaper xp for psi traits, higher mode dot maximums, improved psi point progression, improved attunement range progression, and a higher psi cap, ultimately leading to psionic transcendence as beings of pure thought living on higher noetic planes of existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T23:51:13-08:00","id":1475020,"title":"","content":"Give humanity a few hundred thousand years of psionic evolution and you\u2019ll have a mostly psiad population with potential to reach the highest levels of psi and Mode dots across everything. The Doyen have leap-frogged us a very long way, at the cost of locking into a single Aptitude for full potential.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T06:49:39-08:00","id":1475233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1463938-evolved-psiads?p=1475020#post1475020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Give humanity a few hundred thousand years of psionic evolution and you\u2019ll have a mostly psiad population with potential to reach the highest levels of psi and Mode dots across everything. The Doyen have leap-frogged us a very long way, at the cost of locking into a single Aptitude for full potential.</div> </div> </div> </div>But we're not there yet. And we're probably not getting there any time soon, friendly Nova/Psiad/Psion super-duper geniuses or no. Because the essential choice/opportunity cost between Psiad and Psion is generalist vs. specialist. If you want to do a lot of different things, play a Psiad. If you want to reach the heights of power/perfection in one (fairly broad) Aptitude, play a Psion.<br /> <br /> What we don't really want is some situation where Psiads get boosted to the point that they can go Proxy-level in every Aptitude or something, look at all the Psions and say &quot;Sucks to be you. Shouldn't have gotten dunked.&quot; Or reverse the situation with the &quot;cured&quot; Psion saying &quot;Sucks to be you, should have gotten dunked.&quot; No player should be told &quot;You chose the wrong type of character to play.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T18:30:41-08:00","id":1475276,"title":"","content":"My assumption is that even if Psiad's lose the dot restriction, they're still going to deal with things like lower psi pools and higher xp costs, so at any given level, even an &quot;evolved&quot; psiad would probably come off the worse compared to a psion in his speciality--<br /> And of course there's the gold ring--the fact that psions have an immensely greater ability to team up with each other and get more than the sum of their powers. I'd expect that even <i>fully</i> evolved psiad's probably would still lose out in that area. <br /> <br /> Which of course has a gaming advantage--a psaid, evolved or not, is who you probably want for a one on one game, or a game set where there just aren't a lot of psionics--but if you're talking a group, or a society with support for large numbers of psions, ultimately, psions are probably more powerful. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T21:44:16-08:00","id":1475295,"title":"","content":"If you go by the implied idea that having a single dot in a Vitakinetic mode grants you biological immortality, then Psiad's have Psion's beat for ease of getting access to that dot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T22:31:07-08:00","id":1475299,"title":"","content":"Nope. Auxiliary Mode, one dot: <br /> Psions 8 XP.<br /> Psiads - Primary 8 XP, Secondary 10 XP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T23:10:26-08:00","id":1475301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1463938-evolved-psiads?p=1475233#post1475233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What we don't really want is some situation where Psiads get boosted to the point that they can go Proxy-level in every Aptitude or something, look at all the Psions and say &quot;Sucks to be you. Shouldn't have gotten dunked.&quot; Or reverse the situation with the &quot;cured&quot; Psion saying &quot;Sucks to be you, should have gotten dunked.&quot; No player should be told &quot;You chose the wrong type of character to play.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Clearly the difference in settings is what'll keep that from happening. Same as a Nova in Aberrant versus a Stalwart-type in Adventure. Shame you didn't live a hundred years later- you could have been a living god. <br /> <br /> On a storytelling level, you'd also need to come up with something of a theme for that anything-goes setting. The limited nature of Aptitutes for psions is there to highlight the &quot;Unity&quot; theme of Aeon- you can do amazing things <i>with </i>your fellow psions, but you can't have a character who can do everything well, and you don't have to worry about everyone trying to create that perfectly overpowered character with just the right combination of aptitudes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26448-shalmaneser","name":"Shalmaneser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T04:32:40-08:00","id":1475306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1463938-evolved-psiads?p=1475233#post1475233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But we're not there yet. And we're probably not getting there any time soon, friendly Nova/Psiad/Psion super-duper geniuses or no. Because the essential choice/opportunity cost between Psiad and Psion is generalist vs. specialist. If you want to do a lot of different things, play a Psiad. If you want to reach the heights of power/perfection in one (fairly broad) Aptitude, play a Psion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though to be fair, unless your GM gives you heaps of xp every session for years, even unlocking width+depth in psionic potential doesn't instantly translate to god-like power. It would likely still take you ages to achieve psion-level excellence in one aptitude, let alone several. An evolved Psychomorph of either origin would therefore still have to chose between specialist/generalist. It's just that in theory they don't have to.<br /> <br /> The only immediate advantage I can see to jailbreaking a psychomorph is matching the versatility and QK base powers of psiads with the better psi efficiency and higher max of psions. Nice, but not that gamebreaking ? Of course, YMMV ; I could be mistaken if most other players are actually used to running around with proxy-tier characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26426-trianoma4evah","name":"Trianoma4Evah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T11:36:18-08:00","id":1475340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1463938-evolved-psiads?p=1464417#post1464417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The boundary between BK and VK are thin and diffused (...).</div> </div> </div> </div>Tip: if it has to do with &quot;Perfection&quot; (make the life form a better version of itself) it's VK; if it has to do with &quot;New Potential&quot; (make the life form able to do something that its noetic template CANNOT do), it's BK. (to see about the Aptitudes' subtle domains of action, see Prometheus Unbound)<br /> <br /> So, be able to see better or &quot;fix&quot; eyesight would be VK (humankind noetic template does have eyes and see), but to enable a human to see ultraviolet would be BK (since humankind does not have body cells that are able to see these wavelengths).<br /> <br /> This is why to &quot;boost&quot; Psi trait you need VK (and so, also would be high level VK to &quot;make a Prometheus&quot; manually to a latent) -- but to transform a NON-Latent into a NOW-Latent person I would rule it requires BK: you are practically &quot;giving new organs&quot; to that person, in the sense of the &quot;Psionic surgery&quot; the Doyen did to Proxies (that is, you must give the person the &quot;Psi battery&quot; and the &quot;Psi circuits&quot; their body need to use it -- for more details about these, look at Aexpansion).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}